3. Stage 1: Rational-Arithmetic Audit of the BS26 Proof

The audit reconstructs the BS26 proof in exact rational arithmetic and isolates every occurrence of \gamma\le1/1233 and \chi_k\le1/137. The tasks are:

1. Reconstruct the variational class, the existence and regularity theory, and the Euler–Lagrange system, matching BS26’s normalisation.
2. Re-derive the exterior Sommerfeld comparison and confirm its dependence on \gamma alone.
3. Re-derive the convex nonlinear comparison in P=F(p), and verify the source-mass bound (2.2).
4. Re-derive the quartic coercivity proposition, isolating the role of the truncation p\wedge M, the signed localised Hardy inequality, the role of nuclear repulsion in the molecular case, and the global Hardy device used in the atomic case.
5. Re-derive the final absorption, tracking the dependence of every constant on (\gamma,\chi_k,K).
6. Re-implement the rational-arithmetic verification of all finite inequalities in exact arithmetic, and record the slack margin at each inequality.

The deliverable is a written entry-point map classifying each occurrence of the two restrictions as tight, loose, or structural. This audit determines which Stage 2 extensions are worth pursuing and is independently publishable as a reproducibility and benchmarking contribution.

